  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, nominations 5 January 1926; six nominations for six vacancies, so there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1926, p. 10). Campbell and M'Cartney are marked as old members, the other four as new members. The paper states: 'No election will take place.' Returned unopposed."
